  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "Expanded resources now map cancer biomarkers, GWAS loci and gene-phenotype evidence onto CpG sites, cell types and individual cell lines.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these releases is the integration of heterogeneous evidence layers into searchable, annotated resources. MethMarkerDB 2.0 extends cancer DNA methylation biomarkers to 21 cancer types and adds CpG-level and functional analysis modules. scGWAS-DB links 3,649 GWAS datasets to single-cell atlases spanning 74 human tissues and 1,713 cell types, placing association signals in tissue-resolved cellular context. Gene Expression Nebulas 2.0 expands standardized, manually curated transcriptomic profiles with additional datasets, annotations and functionality. iCellOmics connects genomic, transcriptomic, epigenomic and literature-curated gene-phenotype data for 17 industrially relevant cell lines. The Canine Cancer Genome Atlas harmonizes whole-exome data from 667 canine tumor-normal pairs across 10 histotypes and reports 39 drivers, applying comparable integration logic to veterinary oncology. What is new is the resolution at which evidence is placed: individual CpG sites, specific cell types, or individual cell lines.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
